## Complete Feature Breakdown

### Feature Mode 1: Virtual Try-On (VTON)

#### Step 1 — Garments (`step-garments.tsx`)
- **Product Category**: Clothing or Footwear toggle
- **Gender**: Male, Female, Unisex — affects model selection, garment analysis prompts, and pose filtering
- **Garment Type** (Clothing): Topwear, Bottomwear, Onepiece — filters available poses and adjusts prompt emphasis
- **Footwear Type** (Footwear): 9 types — casual shoes, formal shoes, sneakers, boots, sandals, loafers, heels, sports shoes, slippers
- **Fit** (Clothing only): 8 options — slim, regular, relaxed, oversized, tailored, loose, bodycon, boxy. User-selected fit is AUTHORITATIVE and overrides AI assessment
- **Image Upload**: Drag-drop or click to upload product images (multiple images of the same product for different angles)
- **Complementary Garments** (Clothing only): Additional garment images to include in the outfit (e.g., pants to go with a shirt)
- **Product Info** (Optional): Free-text field for product-specific details (fabric, key features, selling points). In single mode stored as a global string; in bulk mode stored per-folder on `ProductFolder.productInfo`
- **Bulk Mode**: Products organized in folders (`ProductFolder`), each folder represents one product with multiple angle shots and optional product info

#### Step 2 — Styling (`step-styling.tsx`)
- **Background Configuration**:
  - Inspiration image upload (reference for environment)
  - Text description (custom background description)
  - Default studio background (clean e-commerce)
  - Bulk mode: Multiple backgrounds as `BulkBackground` cards — add/remove/edit each
- **Model Selection**:
  - 10 preset AI models: 5 female (Priya, Mei, Emma, Amara, Sofia) + 5 male (Arjun, Kenji, James, Kwame, Carlos) — diverse ethnicities
  - Custom model upload (reference photo)
  - Preset + custom can coexist: preset provides description, custom provides reference photo
  - Filtered by gender selection
  - Bulk mode: Multiple model images as `BulkModelImage` — each with name, file, preview

#### Step 3 — Output (`step-output.tsx`)
- **Aspect Ratio**: 8 options — 1:1, 2:3, 3:2, 3:4, 4:3, 4:5, 9:16, 16:9
- **Pose Selection**: Multi-select from filtered pose library
  - Clothing: 70+ poses across 5 view angles × 7 framing types (from `POSES`)
  - Footwear: 50+ poses split into Product-Only (20+ no-model shots) and On-Model (25+ shots) (from `FOOTWEAR_POSES`)
  - Poses grouped by view angle in the UI
  - Each pose has: `id`, `name`, `description`, `icon`, `viewAngle`, `framing`, `garmentRelevance`, `requiresModel`
- **Per-Pose Accessories**: Each selected pose can have its own set of accessories
  - 18 accessory categories: necklace, pendant, earrings, watch, bracelet, ring, sunglasses, shoes, belt, hat, scarf, handbag, clutch, tie, brooch, cufflinks, anklet, hair-accessory
  - Each accessory can be: AI-chosen (no image — AI picks best match) or exact reference (with uploaded image)

#### Step 4 — Details (`step-details.tsx`)
- **Additional Instructions**: Free-text field for custom instructions passed to prompt generation
- **API Key**: Google Gemini API key input (stored in state, not env vars; show/hide toggle)

#### Step 5 — Generate (`step-generate.tsx`)
- **Generation Summary**: Shows all configured parameters
- **Image Quality**: 1K, 2K (default), 4K
- **Generation Process**:
  1. Creates one `GeneratedResult` per selected pose
  2. For each pose: calls `generateVTONPrompt()` → calls `generateVTONImage()`
  3. Auto-retry on first failure (1 second delay, then retry once)
  4. Concurrency: 5 for single mode, 3 for bulk mode
- **Results Display**: Grid of cards with image preview, status indicator, pose info, expandable prompt
- **Actions**: Download individual images, Infographic editor, Retry failed, Regenerate All
- **Bulk Results**: Grouped by combination with collapsible sections, per-combo ZIP download, master ZIP download

### Feature Mode 2: Model Swap

#### Step 1 — Products (`step-garments.tsx` in model-swap mode)
- Upload existing product photos (images already showing a model wearing clothing)
- **Product Info** (Optional): Free-text field for product-specific details, stored same way as VTON
- Single mode: Upload individual images
- Bulk mode: Organize in folders

#### Step 2 — Styling (`step-styling.tsx` in model-swap mode)
- **Background Mode**: 2 options
  - `keep-same` — Preserve the original background from the product photo
  - `new-background` — Replace with inspiration image, text description, or studio default
- **New Model**: Same selection as VTON (presets + custom upload)
- Bulk mode: Multiple model images, backgrounds configured per-combo

#### Step 3 — Output (`step-output.tsx` in model-swap mode)
- **Aspect Ratio**: Same 8 options
- No pose selection (model swap preserves the original pose)

#### Step 4 — Details (same as VTON)

#### Step 5 — Generate (`step-generate.tsx` in model-swap mode)
- **Single Mode**: One result per source image. Calls `generateModelSwapPrompt()` → `generateModelSwapImage()`
- **Bulk Mode**: One result per source image × model combination (round-robin pairing)
- Same auto-retry, concurrency, download features as VTON

### Infographic Editor (`infographic-editor.tsx` + `infographic-renderer.ts`)
- Opens as a dialog on any generated image
- **USP Badges**: Text + emoji icon + styling
  - 6 badge styles: rounded, pill, square, ribbon, outline, minimal
  - Customizable: text, icon, font size, text color, background color, opacity
  - 18 preset USPs (Pure Cotton, 100% Organic, Sustainable, etc.)
  - 18 preset colors
- **Logo Overlays**: Upload logo image, position, size, opacity
- **Positioning**: 9 overlay positions (3×3 grid) + fine-tune X/Y offset sliders
- **Drag-and-drop**: Reposition elements on canvas with hit-testing
- **Background Dimming**: Overall overlay dimming slider (0-1)
- **Export**: Render to canvas at full resolution and download as PNG

## AI Pipeline — Two-Step Generation

### Step 1: Prompt Generation (Gemini 3 Pro)
```
Model: gemini-3-pro-preview
Config: ThinkingLevel.LOW
Input: System prompt + reference images + parameters
Output: Detailed text prompt (3-5 paragraphs)
```

### Step 2: Image Generation (Nano Banana Pro)
```
Model: gemini-3-pro-image-preview
Config: responseModalities: ["TEXT", "IMAGE"], imageConfig: { aspectRatio, imageSize }
Input: Generated prompt + all reference images
Output: Generated image (base64)
```

### Four AI Functions in `gemini.ts`:
1. `generateVTONPrompt()` — VTON prompt generation (clothing + footwear branches)
2. `generateVTONImage()` — VTON image generation (clothing + footwear branches)
3. `generateModelSwapPrompt()` — Model Swap prompt generation
4. `generateModelSwapImage()` — Model Swap image generation

See `gemini-prompts.mdc` for complete prompt text and logic.

## State Management (`vton-store.ts`)

### Core State
- `mode: AppMode` — "single" | "bulk"
- `featureMode: FeatureMode` — "vton" | "model-swap"
- `currentStep: WizardStep` — 1-5
- `productCategory: ProductCategory` — "clothing" | "footwear"
- `gender: Gender` — "male" | "female" | "unisex"
- `garmentImages: GarmentImage[]` — uploaded product images
- `garmentType: GarmentType` — "topwear" | "bottomwear" | "onepiece"
- `footwearType: FootwearType` — 9 options
- `fit: FitType | null` — 8 options or null (auto-detect)
- `complementaryImages: ComplementaryImage[]` — secondary garments
- `poseAccessories: Record<string, AccessoryItem[]>` — per-pose accessories
- `background: BackgroundConfig` — inspiration image or text
- `selectedModel: AIModel | null` — preset model
- `modelImage: ModelImage | null` — custom uploaded model photo
- `aspectRatio: AspectRatio` — default "3:4"
- `imageQuality: "1K" | "2K" | "4K"` — default "2K"
- `selectedPoses: Pose[]` — multi-select
- `additionalInfo: string` — free text (global instructions for all products)
- `productInfo: string` — free text (product-specific details for single mode)
- `apiKey: string` — Gemini API key

### Bulk State
- `primaryFolders: ProductFolder[]`
- `complementaryFolders: ProductFolder[]`
- `bulkModelImages: BulkModelImage[]`
- `bulkBackgrounds: BulkBackground[]`
- `bulkCombinations: BulkCombination[]` — computed via `useMemo`, round-robin
- `bulkResults: BulkGeneratedResult[]`

### Model Swap State
- `modelSwapBgMode: ModelSwapBackgroundMode` — "keep-same" | "new-background"
- `modelSwapResults: ModelSwapGeneratedResult[]`
- `modelSwapBulkResults: ModelSwapBulkResult[]`
- `modelSwapBulkCombinations: ModelSwapBulkCombination[]` — computed via `useMemo`

### Computed Values
- `hasModel: boolean` — selectedModel !== null || modelImage !== null
- `bulkCombinations` — round-robin: `primary[i] + complementary[i % cgCount] + model[i % modelCount] + background[i % bgCount]`
- `modelSwapBulkCombinations` — round-robin: `primary[i] + model[i % modelCount] + background[i % bgCount]`

### Step Validation (`canProceedToStep`)
**VTON Single:**
- Step 1: always true
- Step 2: garmentImages.length > 0
- Step 3: garmentImages > 0 AND (isFootwear OR hasModel)
- Step 4: garmentImages > 0 AND selectedPoses > 0 AND (isFootwear ? (!anyPoseNeedsModel OR hasModel) : hasModel)
- Step 5: Step 4 conditions AND apiKey.length > 0

**VTON Bulk:**
- Step 1: always true
- Step 2: hasPrimaryProducts
- Step 3: hasPrimaryProducts AND hasModels
- Step 4: hasPrimaryProducts AND hasModels AND selectedPoses > 0
- Step 5: Step 4 conditions AND apiKey.length > 0

**Model Swap Single:**
- Step 1: always true
- Step 2: garmentImages.length > 0
- Step 3: garmentImages > 0 AND hasModel
- Step 4: garmentImages > 0 AND hasModel
- Step 5: Step 4 conditions AND apiKey.length > 0

**Model Swap Bulk:**
- Step 1: always true
- Step 2: hasPrimaryProducts
- Step 3: hasPrimaryProducts AND hasModels
- Step 4: hasPrimaryProducts AND hasModels
- Step 5: Step 4 conditions AND apiKey.length > 0

## Key Conventions

### Component Patterns
- All components are `"use client"` — fully client-side app
- Each wizard step receives `store: VTONStore` prop
- No API routes — all AI calls happen client-side via `@google/genai`
- API key entered by user in Step 4 (not stored in env vars)
- Use `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` for conditional class merging
- Prefer shadcn/ui components from `@/components/ui/` for all UI primitives

### Styling
- Gradient buttons: `bg-gradient-to-r from-orange-600 to-amber-600`
- Rounded corners: `rounded-xl` or `rounded-2xl` for cards
- Card pattern: `rounded-2xl border border-border bg-card p-5`
- Label pattern: `text-xs text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider font-medium`
- Shadow accent: `shadow-lg shadow-orange-500/20`
- Always support dark mode via CSS variables (never hardcode colors)
- Badge colors: Orange for models, Emerald for backgrounds, Secondary for products

### Pose System
- **Clothing Poses** (`POSES`): 70+ poses organized by view angle × framing
  - View Angles: front, side, back, three-quarter-front, three-quarter-back
  - Framing: full-body, three-quarter, mid-thigh, waist-up, bust-up, hip-down, knee-down
  - `garmentRelevance`: filters which garment types each pose applies to
- **Footwear Poses** (`FOOTWEAR_POSES`): 50+ poses split into:
  - Product-Only (`requiresModel: false`): 20+ shots with no human model — front, side, back, ¾ angles, top-down, sole view; single shoe and pair variants
  - On-Model: 25+ shots — full-body, hip-down, knee-down, feet-closeup framings across all view angles
  - View Angles: front, side, back, three-quarter-front, three-quarter-back, top-down, bottom
  - Framing adds: `product-only`, `feet-closeup`

### Generation Flow
1. User configures all parameters across steps 1-4
2. Step 5: User clicks "Generate"
3. App creates result objects (one per pose for VTON, one per source image for Model Swap)
4. For each result:
   a. Status → "generating-prompt"
   b. Call prompt generation function with all parameters
   c. Status → "generating-image"
   d. Call image generation function with prompt + all reference images
   e. Status → "completed" (or "error")
5. On first failure: auto-retry after 1 second (status → "auto-retrying")
6. On second failure: status → "error" with error message
7. Manual retry available for failed results

### Bulk Mode
- Products organized in folders (`ProductFolder`)
- Round-robin pairing: `primary[i] + complementary[i % cgCount] + model[i % modelCount] + background[i % bgCount]`
- Multiple backgrounds: `bulkBackgrounds` array of `BulkBackground` — each has `id`, `name`, `config: BackgroundConfig`
- If no bulk backgrounds configured, default studio background used
- Backgrounds configured in Step 2 via card-based UI
- Concurrency: 3 for bulk, 5 for single
- Results grouped by combination in UI with collapsible sections
- Download: Individual, per-combo ZIP, master ZIP (nested folders by product name)

### Infographic Editor
- Canvas-based rendering (`infographic-renderer.ts`)
- Supports USP badges (text + icon + styling) and logo overlays
- Drag-and-drop repositioning with hit-testing
- 9 overlay positions + fine-tune offset sliders
- 6 badge styles: rounded, pill, square, ribbon, outline, minimal
- 18 preset USPs and 18 preset colors
- Export as PNG at full resolution

## Adding New Features

### New wizard steps
Add to `WIZARD_STEPS` (and `MODEL_SWAP_WIZARD_STEPS` if applicable) in constants.ts, create `step-*.tsx`, update `vton-wizard.tsx` switch, update `canProceedToStep()` in store

### New gender options
Add to `GENDER_OPTIONS` in constants.ts, update `Gender` type in types.ts

### New clothing poses
Add to `POSES` array in constants.ts with correct `viewAngle`, `framing`, `garmentRelevance`

### New footwear poses
Add to `FOOTWEAR_POSES` in constants.ts — set `requiresModel: false` for product-only shots

### New footwear types
Add to `FOOTWEAR_TYPE_OPTIONS` in constants.ts, update `FootwearType` type in types.ts

### New product categories
Add to `PRODUCT_CATEGORY_OPTIONS` in constants.ts, update `ProductCategory` type, add category-specific prompt branches in gemini.ts

### New accessories
Add to `ACCESSORY_CATEGORIES` in constants.ts, update `AccessoryCategory` type

### New AI models
Add to `AI_MODELS` in constants.ts

### New fit options
Add to `FIT_OPTIONS` in constants.ts, update `FitType` type

### New aspect ratios
Add to `ASPECT_RATIOS` in constants.ts, update `AspectRatio` type

### New feature modes
Add to `FEATURE_MODE_OPTIONS` in constants.ts, update `FeatureMode` type, add mode-specific wizard steps, prompts, and generation logic

### New background modes
Update `BackgroundMode` / `ModelSwapBackgroundMode` in types.ts, add options in constants.ts, update prompt logic in gemini.ts

## File Modification Rules

- **NEVER** edit files in `src/components/ui/` directly — use `npx shadcn@latest add <component>`
- **ALWAYS** update `src/lib/types.ts` when adding new data structures
- **ALWAYS** update `src/lib/constants.ts` when adding new configurable options
- **ALWAYS** keep prompts in `src/lib/gemini.ts` — do not scatter AI prompts across components
- **ALWAYS** update `canProceedToStep()` in the store when changing step validation logic
- **ALWAYS** update both `WIZARD_STEPS` and `MODEL_SWAP_WIZARD_STEPS` if the step change applies to both feature modes
- **ALWAYS** clean up `URL.createObjectURL()` references with `URL.revokeObjectURL()` when removing images from state
- **ALWAYS** maintain round-robin logic in `useMemo` computed combinations when adding new pairing dimensions
